<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>智能新闻| smithsonianmag.com</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/rss/smart-news/</link><description>智能新闻的 RSS 提要</description><lastBuildDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 15:42:02 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>这种古老的昆虫有 24 条腿，可以帮助解释现代虫子的祖先如何占领这片土地</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-ancient-insect-had-24-legs-and-could-help-explain-how-the-ancestors-of-modern-day-bugs-took-over-the-land-180989420/</link><description>一种生活在 3.24 亿年前、此前未被描述的生物似乎是生活在陆地和海洋之间的过渡物种。它可以帮助研究人员填补甲壳类动物如何进化为昆虫的化石记录中8000万年的空白</description><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-ancient-insect-had-24-legs-and-could-help-explain-how-the-ancestors-of-modern-day-bugs-took-over-the-land-180989420/</guid></item><item><title>在太多雄性树蛙的求偶叫声中，雌性树蛙经历“选择过载”</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/female-treefrogs-experience-choice-overload-amid-too-many-mating-calls-from-males-180989411/</link><description>一项研究表明，面对一大群潜在的配偶，雌性科普灰树蛙可能会因众多的选择而不知所措，难以做出谨慎的决定</description><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 13:42:53 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/female-treefrogs-experience-choice-overload-amid-too-many-mating-calls-from-males-180989411/</guid></item><item><title>亨利八世的一座堡垒中的石头被隐藏在众目睽睽之下一个多世纪了。新研究表明维多利亚时代的人将它们重新用作建筑材料</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/stones-from-one-of-henry-viiis-fortresses-spent-more-than-a-century-hidden-in-plain-sight-new-research-suggests-the-victorians-repurposed-them-as-building-materials-180989427/</link><description>最近发现的档案记录表明，19 世纪末建造多佛城堡警官门扩建部分的工人重复使用了都铎时代桑当城堡的碎片</description><pubDate>Tue, 01 Sep 2026 12:52:03 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/stones-from-one-of-henry-viiis-fortresses-spent-more-than-a-century-hidden-in-plain-sight-new-research-suggests-the-victorians-repurposed-them-as-building-materials-180989427/</guid></item><item><title>是什么引发了尼泊尔​​和西藏的毁灭性洪水？未来还会发生更多洪水吗？这是科学家迄今为止所知道的</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/what-triggered-the-devastating-floods-in-nepal-and-tibet-and-are-we-due-for-more-in-the-future-heres-what-scientists-know-so-far-180989426/</link><description>自然灾害研究人员怀疑，涉及冰川的山体滑坡引发了这一事件，他们表示，由于人为造成的气候变化，可能会发生更多事件</description><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 20:50:28 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/what-triggered-the-devastating-floods-in-nepal-and-tibet-and-are-we-due-for-more-in-the-future-heres-what-scientists-know-so-far-180989426/</guid></item><item><title>参观见证了英格兰最伟大剧变的古代人的数字重建面孔</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/see-the-digitally-reconstructed-face-of-an-ancient-man-who-witnessed-englands-greatest-upheaval-180989425/</link><description>这位所谓的“征服者”于 1079 年被埋葬在英国，此时距离征服者威廉统治仅十多年。研究人员最近分析了骨骼的 DNA 和牙齿，以更多地了解他</description><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 20:35:48 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/see-the-digitally-reconstructed-face-of-an-ancient-man-who-witnessed-englands-greatest-upheaval-180989425/</guid></item><item><title>挪威的一座新博物馆将游客带入鲸鱼的世界——从真人大小的逆戟鲸到沉浸式水下展览</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-new-museum-in-northern-norway-is-bringing-visitors-into-the-world-of-whales-from-life-size-orcas-to-immersive-underwater-exhibits-180989421/</link><description>The Whale 将于 2027 年开业，将通过艺术、讲故事、声音和建筑来探索鲸鱼的科学、行为、进化和文化历史</description><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 17:57:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-new-museum-in-northern-norway-is-bringing-visitors-into-the-world-of-whales-from-life-size-orcas-to-immersive-underwater-exhibits-180989421/</guid></item><item><title>窃贼在一场“超级专业”的博物馆抢劫中仅用了四分钟就窃取了 3000 年历史的宝藏</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/thieves-steal-3000-year-old-treasure-in-a-super-professional-museum-heist-that-took-only-four-minutes-180989418/</link><description>西班牙维耶纳当地考古博物馆的数十件古代文物消失后，官员们感到震惊。盗贼只留下了青铜时代宝藏的几件</description><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 17:11:11 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/thieves-steal-3000-year-old-treasure-in-a-super-professional-museum-heist-that-took-only-four-minutes-180989418/</guid></item><item><title>《奥德赛》译者艾米丽·威尔逊在称克里斯托弗·诺兰的大片“深渊”后重新开始</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/emily-wilson-will-completely-re-translate-homers-odyssey-after-calling-christopher-nolan-blockbuster-film-abysmal-180989423/</link><description>威尔逊首个广受好评的译本出版近十年后，她正在以全新的方式解读荷马的古希腊史诗</description><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 16:21:17 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/emily-wilson-will-completely-re-translate-homers-odyssey-after-calling-christopher-nolan-blockbuster-film-abysmal-180989423/</guid></item><item><title>你会吃用升级塑料制成的饼干吗？科学家提出一种在极端环境下处理废物和提供食物的新方法</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/would-you-eat-a-cookie-made-from-upcycled-plastics-scientists-propose-a-new-way-to-deal-with-waste-and-provide-food-in-extreme-environments-180989413/</link><description>一组研究人员对酵母进行了编程，将分解的塑料和农业废物转化为名为 µBites 的甜食。它们可能会在深空任务或灾区派上用场，尽管一些批评者说这种食物不切实际</description><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 15:42:33 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/would-you-eat-a-cookie-made-from-upcycled-plastics-scientists-propose-a-new-way-to-deal-with-waste-and-provide-food-in-extreme-environments-180989413/</guid></item><item><title>丹麦考古学家在维京时代坟墓中发现了保存有 1,300 年历史的稀有衣物碎片</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/archaeologists-in-denmark-discover-rare-fragments-of-1300-year-old-clothing-preserved-inside-viking-age-grave-180989419/</link><description>研究人员在一对金属胸针上发现了织物痕迹。当配件腐蚀时，它们会释放出金属盐，无意中使织物保存了几个世纪</description><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 14:52:27 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/archaeologists-in-denmark-discover-rare-fragments-of-1300-year-old-clothing-preserved-inside-viking-age-grave-180989419/</guid></item><item><title>来认识一下新发现的毛茸茸的鱼种，以《芝麻街》中的 Snuffleupagus 先生命名</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/meet-the-newly-discovered-fuzzy-fish-species-named-after-mr-snuffleupagus-from-sesame-street-180988774/</link><description>鬼海龙邋遢的外表可能使它看起来像漂浮的藻类，使其能够融入环境。自二十多年前首次发现这种奇怪的生物以来，研究人员多年来一直在寻找这种奇怪的生物</description><pubDate>Mon, 31 Aug 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/meet-the-newly-discovered-fuzzy-fish-species-named-after-mr-snuffleupagus-from-sesame-street-180988774/</guid></item><item><title>美国宇航局南希·格雷斯·罗马太空望远镜发射寻找系外行星并解开暗物质和暗能量之谜</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/nasas-nancy-grace-roman-space-telescope-launches-to-find-exoplanets-and-unravel-mysteries-of-dark-matter-and-dark-energy-180989268/</link><description>新天文台将在五年内完成三项宇宙调查，尽管它的设计运行时间至少是原来的两倍。它的数据可能会改变科学家对宇宙的基本理解</description><pubDate>Sun, 30 Aug 2026 11:26:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/nasas-nancy-grace-roman-space-telescope-launches-to-find-exoplanets-and-unravel-mysteries-of-dark-matter-and-dark-energy-180989268/</guid></item><item><title>森林在古代全球变暖事件中表现不佳，为当今的气候变化提供了一个“警示”故事</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/forests-didnt-fare-well-during-an-ancient-global-warming-event-offering-a-cautionary-tale-about-todays-climate-change-180989353/</link><description>一项研究表明，5600 万年前的一场剧烈的全球变暖事件导致现代怀俄明州的森林失去了约 60% 的树冠覆盖率，并且花了 10 万多年的时间才恢复过来</description><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 18:43:58 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/forests-didnt-fare-well-during-an-ancient-global-warming-event-offering-a-cautionary-tale-about-todays-climate-change-180989353/</guid></item><item><title>在西班牙洞穴深处，罗马妇女可能崇拜一位神秘的女神</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/deep-inside-spanish-cave-roman-women-may-have-worshipped-mysterious-goddess-180989414/</link><description>瓦伦西亚的科瓦德莱多内斯 (Cova de les Dones) 以其旧石器时代艺术而闻名，这里还拥有一座罗马圣所，研究人员称，那里的女性似乎在崇拜女性神的过程中发挥了积极作用</description><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 18:43:43 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/deep-inside-spanish-cave-roman-women-may-have-worshipped-mysterious-goddess-180989414/</guid></item><item><title>研究表明，历史污染，而不是当前的工业排放，损害了世界上最大、最古老的古代岩石艺术收藏</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/historical-pollution-not-current-industrial-emissions-damaged-worlds-largest-oldest-collection-ancient-rock-art-180989416/</link><description>研究人员表示，过去接触二氧化硫可能是恩加达-恩加利人数万年前创造的穆鲁朱加岩画孔隙度增加的原因</description><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 18:04:36 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/historical-pollution-not-current-industrial-emissions-damaged-worlds-largest-oldest-collection-ancient-rock-art-180989416/</guid></item><item><title>这颗恒星以破纪录的速度绕我们银河系的中心运行，可能有助于揭开有关那里巨大黑洞的秘密</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-star-orbits-our-galaxys-heart-at-a-record-breaking-speed-and-could-help-uncover-secrets-about-the-behemoth-black-hole-there-180989393/</link><description>Speedster 的行驶速度高达每小时 5600 万英里，约为光速的 8%。它还非常接近银河系中心的超大质量黑洞</description><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 15:45:08 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/this-star-orbits-our-galaxys-heart-at-a-record-breaking-speed-and-could-help-uncover-secrets-about-the-behemoth-black-hole-there-180989393/</guid></item><item><title>一位房东在一间空置的公寓里发现了一幅奇怪的印刷品。原来是失踪八年的毕加索原作</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-landlord-found-a-peculiar-print-hanging-in-a-vacant-apartment-it-turned-out-to-be-an-original-picasso-print-that-had-been-missing-for-eight-years-180989417/</link><description>2018 年，当“斗牛士”从密尔沃基一家美术馆消失时，店主不知道是否还能再次看到它。发现这幅蚀刻画的男子本月早些时候将其交给了警方</description><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 15:37:31 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/a-landlord-found-a-peculiar-print-hanging-in-a-vacant-apartment-it-turned-out-to-be-an-original-picasso-print-that-had-been-missing-for-eight-years-180989417/</guid></item><item><title>当水果稀缺时，这些猴子就会捕食动物。这种行为可能为人类食肉习惯的起源提供线索</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/when-fruit-is-scarce-these-monkeys-hunt-animals-the-behavior-may-offer-clues-about-the-origins-of-humans-meat-eating-habits-180989412/</link><description>巴西东北部的胡须卷尾猴通常吃植物性食物，但当这些来源有限时，它们就会转向小型脊椎动物。我们的祖先可能也做了同样的事，最终让掠夺行为在我们的血统中更频繁地传承下去</description><pubDate>Fri, 28 Aug 2026 14:00:00 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/when-fruit-is-scarce-these-monkeys-hunt-animals-the-behavior-may-offer-clues-about-the-origins-of-humans-meat-eating-habits-180989412/</guid></item><item><title>蜗牛可以根据自己的需要使粘液变得粘稠、滑滑、泡沫状或坚硬。这是他们如何调整多用途粘液的方法</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/snails-can-make-their-slime-sticky-slippery-foamy-or-hard-depending-on-their-needs-heres-how-they-tweak-their-multipurpose-mucus-180989361/</link><description>这些生物可以改变多功能物质中钙和胶原蛋白的比例，从而改变蛋白质结构。不同的纹理可以帮助蜗牛滑行、攀爬或保护自己</description><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 20:04:47 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/snails-can-make-their-slime-sticky-slippery-foamy-or-hard-depending-on-their-needs-heres-how-they-tweak-their-multipurpose-mucus-180989361/</guid></item><item><title>经过十年的修复工作，1,800 名志愿者将一座 400 吨重的日本城堡拉回原位</title><link>https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/1800-people-pull-a-400-ton-japanese-castle-keep-back-toward-its-original-location-after-a-decade-of-restoration-work-180989401/</link><description>帮助移动城堡的机会吸引了来自日本和国外的数千份申请。成群结队的彩票中奖者轮流拉动连接在巨大结构上的粗绳子</description><pubDate>Thu, 27 Aug 2026 19:43:03 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.smithsonianmag.com/smart-news/1800-people-pull-a-400-ton-japanese-castle-keep-back-toward-its-original-location-after-a-decade-of-restoration-work-180989401/</guid></item></channel></rss>